{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Because</b> the sages of Spain found hostility in the concealment of the yod, and it is written וְאָיַבְתִּי את איביךָ. Also the hunt of an animal (Leviticus 17:13) says צַיָדִים (Jeremiah 16:16), and the case of judging they did not judge, and HaShem was לְדַיָּן (1 Samuel 24:16). Therefore they said: there is no verb fewer than three letters; therefore איבה is from עלומי העין."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "Reading לא דנו literally; the argument turns on forms that appear to derive from two-letter roots, which the Spanish sages resolve by positing a concealed third letter."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:43.084930559Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}